{"tool_name":"dogsite3","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"dogsite3","home":"https://www.zbh.uni-hamburg.de/en/forschung/amd/software/dogsite3.html","license":"Other","summary":"DoGSite3 was developed for predicting robust and reliable small molecule binding sites and computing their geometrical and chemical descriptors. It is based on the grid-based DoGSite algorithm for predicting pockets and their sub-pockets. The new tool is largely rotation- and translation-invariant due to a normalization procedure before binding site prediction. Known ligands in the structure can be used to bias the grid by sufficiently buried ligand fragments. The output encompasses novel chemical binding site descriptors considering solvent accessibility. Compared to its predecessor, it shows increased robustness through comprehensive parameter optimization. DoGSite3 runs finish within seconds.","addition_date":"2025-12-15T10:10:43.359638Z","last_update_date":"2026-06-16T12:28:18.377473Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web API","Web service"],"collections":["de.NBI","de.NBI-biodata"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:dogsite3","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"email":"pplus.zbh@uni-hamburg.de","name":"ProteinsPlus Support","note":"Primary Contact for Web Service Issues","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"software.zbh@uni-hamburg.de","name":"NAOMI ChemBio Suite Support","note":"Primary Contact for Standalone Tool Issues","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"University of Hamburg, ZBH - Center for Bioinformatics","rorid":"00g30e956","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://proteins.plus/help/index"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["MelanieZBH","ehrt"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"UniProt accession","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3021"}},{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"},"format":[{"te